[00:15.73]Read the story and think about the differences between Li Lele and Wang Haoran`s body language.阅读故事，思考李乐乐和王浩然的肢体语言有何不同。
[00:23.26]Body language matters.肢体语言很重要。
[00:26.51]Li Lele and Wang Haoran are university students. They both have part-time jobs at a travel company.李乐乐和王浩然是大学生，他们都在一家旅游公司做兼职。
[00:37.26]A well-dressed lady entered the office.一位衣着得体的女士走进了办公室。
[00:44.57]She looked at Li Lele and Wang Haoran, and then walked over to Lele.她看了看李乐乐和王浩然，然后走向了乐乐。
[00:51.57]Lele looked excited.乐乐看起来很兴奋。
[00:54.57]"Good morning, madam," she said cheerfully.“早上好，女士，”她兴高采烈地说。
[00:58.46]Haoran sighed and walked away.浩然叹了口气，走开了。
[01:02.41]"What`s the matter?" asked Mr Yang, the boss.“怎么了？”老板杨先生问道。
[01:09.60]"People always choose Lele instead of me. I don`t understand."“人们总是选乐乐而不选我，我不明白。”
[01:15.90]"I do. It`s the way you communicate."“我明白，问题出在你的沟通方式上。”
[01:20.06]"How can that be?" Haoran asked. "I don`t get a chance to speak."“怎么会呢？”浩然问，“我都没机会说话。”
[01:27.17]"Communicating means more than just speaking. Your body language is important too."“沟通不仅仅意味着说话，你的肢体语言也很重要。”
[01:34.81]"Body language?"“肢体语言？”
[01:37.30]"It`s the way you stand and sit. It`s your gestures, and the expressions on your face. “它是你站立和坐姿的样子，是你的手势，还有你脸上的表情。
[01:45.41]Your whole appearance communicates things."你的整体形象都在传递信息。”
[01:49.10]"You don`t give people a good impression, Haoran. “浩然，你给人的印象不好。
[01:53.39]You look down. You never smile, and you don`t turn your head towards them."你总是低着头，从不微笑，也不把脸转向他们。”
[02:00.64]"Look at Lele. She`s holding her head up. She always smiles and looks friendly. “看看乐乐，她昂首挺胸，总是面带微笑，看起来很友善。
[02:09.04]Her body language is making people feel welcome, so they go to her for help."她的肢体语言让人们感到受欢迎，所以大家都去找她帮忙。”
[02:16.24]Haoran observed Lele carefully for a while, and then decided to improve his own body language.浩然仔细观察了乐乐一会儿，然后决定改进自己的肢体语言。
[02:24.52]He sat up straight and tried smiling at people.他坐直了身子，试着对人们微笑。
[02:28.97]Minutes later, a beautiful girl entered.几分钟后，一位漂亮的女孩走了进来。
[02:33.81]She walked over to Haoran.她走向了浩然。
[02:39.22]A few moments later, she left with a smile.片刻之后，她微笑着离开了。
[02:43.90]Mr Yang came over at once and said: "You made a good impression on her, Haoran."杨先生立刻走过来，说：“浩然，你给她留下了很好的印象。”
[02:53.90]"That was my sister," said Haoran. "She wanted to remind me that tomorrow is her birthday."“那是我妹妹，”浩然说，“她是来提醒我明天是她的生日。”

